{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5093cd17-9fab-5758-9081-55418077cd05",
    "name": "Home Dashboard API (v1)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Mobile app API of the home dashboard (`/api/v1`).\n\n1. Import the collection and the **Home Dashboard** environment, select the environment and set `password`.\n2. Run **Auth > Login**. Every other request then sends `Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}`, refreshed automatically before it expires.\n3. The *List* requests fill `device_id`, `tuya_id`, `camera_id`, etc. with the first item, so the action requests work straight away.\n\n**WebSocket** (live updates): Postman > New > WebSocket, URL `ws://<server>:8811/api/v1/ws?token=<stream token>` (get one with **Auth > Stream token**). Messages: `devices`, `tuya`, `appliances`, `events`, `event`.\n\nInteractive docs: `{{base_url}}/docs` (browser login)."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Keeps the Bearer token fresh: refreshes it a minute before it expires (refresh tokens rotate,",
          "// so the new one is stored), and fetches a stream token for requests that use ?token={{stream_token}}.",
          "const url = pm.request.url.toString();",
          "const base = pm.variables.get(\"base_url\");",
          "if (/\\/auth\\/(login|refresh)$/.test(url)) return;",
          "",
          "function refreshAccess(next) {",
          "  const rt = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"refresh_token\");",
          "  const exp = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"access_expires_at\") || 0);",
          "  if (!rt || exp - Date.now() > 60000) return next();",
          "  pm.sendRequest({ url: base + \"/api/v1/auth/refresh\", method: \"POST\",",
          "    header: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },",
          "    body: { mode: \"raw\", raw: JSON.stringify({ refresh_token: rt }) } }, (err, res) => {",
          "    if (!err && res.code === 200) {",
          "      const t = res.json();",
          "      pm.collectionVariables.set(\"access_token\", t.access_token);",
          "      pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refresh_token\", t.refresh_token);",
          "      pm.collectionVariables.set(\"access_expires_at\", String(Date.now() + t.expires_in * 1000));",
          "    } else {",
          "      console.warn(\"Token refresh failed, run Auth > Login again\", err || res.code);",
          "    }",
          "    next();",
          "  });",
          "}",
          "",
          "function streamToken() {",
          "  if (!url.includes(\"{{stream_token}}\") && !url.includes(\"token=\")) return;",
          "  const exp = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"stream_expires_at\") || 0);",
          "  if (pm.collectionVariables.get(\"stream_token\") && exp - Date.now() > 30000) return;",
          "  pm.sendRequest({ url: base + \"/api/v1/auth/stream-token\", method: \"GET\",",
          "    header: { Authorization: \"Bearer \" + pm.collectionVariables.get(\"access_token\") } }, (err, res) => {",
          "    if (!err && res.code === 200) {",
          "      const t = res.json();",
          "      pm.collectionVariables.set(\"stream_token\", t.token);",
          "      pm.collectionVariables.set(\"stream_expires_at\", String(Date.now() + t.expires_in * 1000));",
          "    }",
          "  });",
          "}",
          "",
          "refreshAccess(streamToken);"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
